Open enrollment within Wyoming school 25LSO-0329, 1.0
districts.
FISCAL NOTE
The fiscal impact is indeterminable.
This bill provides for the board of trustees of each school district to provide for
the enrollment of any pupil in any public school within the pupil's resident school
district, except in cases where a school does not have sufficient capacity or the
pupil has been suspended or expelled.
The Department of Education indicates this bill may create indeterminable
expenditure increases from the Public School Foundation Program Account in the form
of school district allowable transportation expenditures that are reimbursed 100
percent and in the form of increased school district foundation program amounts
from the K-12 education resource block grant model, which are based on the unique
characteristics of each school and school district, including student enrollment.
